#!/usr/bin/env python3
# cs1gk -- CHARACTER SHEET 1 GAUGE KEEP. Measures a persona / character sheet against the shop's own
#          rules for one, so a sheet written in a hurry cannot drift from the program quietly:
#            gw7's shape   (c4/h/MODEL-gw7.md s4-6, c4/h/PERSONA-gw7.md as the reference instance):
#                          fleshing · garb ("what I wear") · the bench (tools & accessories WITH usage) ·
#                          what I hold (responsibility / possession, a table) · a journal in the persona's
#                          own voice · a GROW receipt + LENS reflection; tonal growth only with BOTH
#                          evidence AND the journal story.
#            the METHOD    (c4/h/METHOD-lens-and-granule-ring.md): a sheet NAMES the LENS guards it elects
#                          (hold-four-views · break-your-own-claim · ground-in-durables · compost-a-loss ·
#                          drift-fund).
#            dungeon       (modelthisbook/news/METHOD-dungeon-modeling.md; dungeon-mode's Character
#                          Sample Detail Sheet): a TSV sidecar with cs-intrinsics (incl. gold + special),
#                          cs-skills, cs-posessions; DOUBLE-ENTRY = every row names its source counterpart.
#            NEWS          any sheet that leans on a roll / LENS / seed / fate carries the mark:
#                          "for fiction or analysis -- no ship dates or licensing or publication dates
#                          specifically defined".
#            corpus        the sheet is registered in PERSONA-CORPUS.md (voice nodes with sources).
#            duplicates    --twin DIR: the same-named sheet elsewhere is SAME / DIVERGED / ABSENT (mtime
#                          is never a tiebreaker; both shas are printed).
#          It MEASURES (words: OK · WARN · FAULT · NOTVISIBLE) and never edits a sheet. --diagram emits a
#          canonical diagram document (bin/dc1sv renders it) of the sheet's TSV as a graph-paper table.
#
